# Diagnose loop

- **Rules own protocol and evidence:** board merge, safety, applicability, which OEM phrases may be appended ([ADR-0031](docs/adr/0031-structured-diagnostic-state.md), [ADR-0034](docs/adr/0034-diagnose-nlu-split.md)).
- **Do not** add `when_user_says` slang so search can understand the user. **Do not** replace diagnose with a rule-only expert-system tree.
- **Do not** implement unconstrained query rewrite. R18 is closed-set labels that pick a retrieve family ([ADR-0039](docs/adr/0039-diagnose-retrieve-labels.md)); `add_to_search` stays literature text.
- `_retrieval_query` / `acks.py` remain the offline fallback. Do not grow those detectors as the product strategy. The classify call may return a label only — never a search string.
- Board merge harvests numbered checks and `TEST #N` names from the prior assistant turn (one per line or inline `1. … 2. …`). Classify `ack` / `still_unresolved` counts as progress even when `acks.py` does not match. After the user clears a category, do not restart that category from the first listed cause. Name a See TEST #N pointer once; after the user confirms it, **close by rule** — do not call generate to repeat that TEST.
- Progress follow-ups (`ack` / `still_unresolved`) **reuse** the last evidence pack. Do not call `search()` to be helpful. `new_symptom` and `mid_cycle_stop` still search ([ADR-0043](docs/adr/0043-session-evidence-reuse.md)).
- The `/ui` session tally is a read-only view of the board ([ADR-0044](docs/adr/0044-diagnose-session-tally.md), [ADR-0045](docs/adr/0045-diagnose-tally-symptom-trail.md)). A corrected problem appends a span and keeps checks with that problem. Do not turn it into a clickable flowchart, thumbs, or persisted session state.
